% A zero divisor in a test of constants is an evaluation error too, met
% once, before the rule reads anything: the evaluation stops with no rows
% and a nonzero exit, naming the rule, however many tuples the rule would
% have gone on to read.
v(1). v(2). v(3).
w(a).

bad(X) :- w(a), 1 < 12 / 0, v(X).

bad(X)?
